<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7421" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναρρύω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥύω,
		ἐρύω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>draw</i> the
			victim's head <i>back</i> so as to cut the throat,
			like Homer's <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐερύω</span>:
			hence, <i>sacrifice,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				139
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				13.81
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				395
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Med.
			, aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνερρυσάμην,</span>
			<i>draw back, rescue,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχὴν ἀ. παθέων</span>
			<i>from</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				23
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πόλεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>VP</u>
					7.33
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἧτταν</span>
			<i>repair</i> a defeat, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				5.46
			</span></i> codd.:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνερρύσθησαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Just.
					<u>Nov.</u>
					115.3.13
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
